cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite both the paper and the software."
type: software
title: "beyond32: superconducting pairing channels of the icosahedral group"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-05
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/psldm/beyond32"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22335534"
authors:
  - family-names: Moss
    given-names: Eva
abstract: >-
  Exact (sympy, Q(sqrt5)) group theory of the icosahedral group I, I_h and 2I for
  superconducting pairing channels: character tables, branching of spherical harmonics,
  basis functions, Molien series and the S^3/2I spectrum, restrictions to approximant
  subgroups, permutation representations on cluster shells, double-group branching, and
  the Ginzburg-Landau invariants, weak-coupling minima, symmetry-fixed states and
  enforced nodes of the T1, T2, G and H channels; plus the dodecagonal group D12.
keywords:
  - icosahedral group
  - quasicrystal
  - superconductivity
  - Ginzburg-Landau theory
  - representation theory
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Beyond the 32: Superconducting Pairing Channels of the Icosahedral Group -- Classification, Approximant Branching, and Ginzburg-Landau Theory for Quasicrystals"
  authors:
    - family-names: Moss
      given-names: Eva
  year: 2026
